{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MarkovZClassicalCoincidence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovZClassicalCoincidence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zCsub_eq_zDsub_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zCsub_eq_zDsub_iff","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZClassicalCoincidence.lean#L103-L135","doc":"**The coincidence is isolated.**  For `s > 0`, the two Markov parameters\nagree exactly at `s = 1` (`q = 1`) and nowhere else.\n\nThe forward direction is the sharp form of `decayLadder_zC_not_jones`: that\ntheorem rules out `s > 1`, while this rules out every positive `s ≠ 1`,\nincluding the interval `0 < s < 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.coincidenceLocus_cofactor_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.coincidenceLocus_cofactor_pos","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZClassicalCoincidence.lean#L97-L101","doc":"The cofactor of the coincidence locus is strictly positive for `s > 0`\n(all coefficients positive). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zCsub_eq_zDsub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zCsub_eq_zDsub_one","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZClassicalCoincidence.lean#L88-L93","doc":"**The classical-limit coincidence.**  The two conventions define the *same*\nMarkov parameter at `q = 1`.  This is why a ladder coefficient obtained as a\n`q = 1` evaluation of a Markov-trace invariant — `c₃ = J_Hopf(1) = −2` — is\nunmoved by the C→D ruling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zDsub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zDsub_one","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZClassicalCoincidence.lean#L84-L86","doc":"At the classical point `q = 1` (`s = 1`) convention D gives `1/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zCsub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zCsub_one","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZClassicalCoincidence.lean#L80-L82","doc":"At the classical point `q = 1` (`s = 1`) convention C gives `1/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zDsub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zDsub","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZClassicalCoincidence.lean#L76-L78","doc":"Convention **D** Markov parameter (canonical) in the substrate variable:\n`z_D = s⁶/(s⁴+1)` (i.e. `q³/(q²+1)` at `q = s²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zCsub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zCsub","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZClassicalCoincidence.lean#L71-L74","doc":"Convention **C** Markov parameter in the substrate variable: `z_C = s/(s²+1)`\n(i.e. `√q/(q+1)` at `q = s²`).  Excised as canonical by the 2026-08-15 ruling;\nretained here only to state the comparison. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.coincidenceLocus_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.coincidenceLocus_factor","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovZClassicalCoincidence.lean#L58-L67","doc":"The denominator-cleared coincidence locus of `z_C` and `z_D`, factored.\n\nThis is the identity behind `decayLadder_zC_not_jones`'s `s⁷ + s⁵ = s⁴ + 1`:\nthe polynomial has `s = 1` as a root, and the cofactor has all-positive\ncoefficients.  Pure `CommRing` content — no ordering, no archimedean structure\n(AGENTS.md §7c). ","signatureChunk":0}]}